{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{\\sin }^{2}⁡t+6{\\cos }^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{\\cos }^{2}⁡t+({\\sin }^{2}⁡t+{\\cos }^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{\\cos }^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =6{\\cos }^{2}⁡t-6{\\sin }^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =6({\\cos }^{2}⁡t-{\\sin }^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{5{\\cos }^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{5{\\cos }^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]
